Patch 139 — SELECT PLAYER (cc33 list dialog) bit-identical: bg composite + save/restore + list text + selection.

Resolves the two remaining SELECT PLAYER blockers to AE=0 (native + wasm bit-identical), all asm-verified
vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin + re_out/fist_mga_image.bin:

BLOCKER 1 (bg does not composite / flat olive) — ROOT CAUSE = FUN_0000_cdc4, the scrollbar-TRACK paint
method, ran base-lost with every MGAVIDEO method-vector arg dropped, so its [0x60a]=1091 fills used
codegen-garbage bx/al -> a WILD inverted rect (rows underflow to 65501) filled with a garbage colour
(0x30 olive) that WIPED the whole screen every frame.  This is ALSO Blocker 2: the wild write's target
depended on the garbage bx, so it SEGV'd ~1/8 (crash-free under -ftrivial-auto-var-init=pattern, where
bx=0xAAAA lands inside g_mem).  cdc4 reconstructed instruction-for-instruction (asm 0xcdc4..0xce36):
recover the element from DGROUP:0x3e08, box outline [0x61a]=11db(2), scratch rect @DGROUP:0xe873, the two
[0x60a]=1091 track fills (colour 0) + the [0x6b4]=26a1 thumb sprite (id 0x108+a86d).  NB the scratch
a875 store is a 16-bit WORD (asm `mov [0xe875],ax`); Ghidra's iRam0002a875 int (4-byte) store zeroed the
adjacent a877 -> a second wild fill; faithful 16-bit store.

Save/RESTORE — the SELECT PLAYER (cc33) dialog is supposed to RESTORE the terrain-only menu backdrop
(saved by the menu's e38a(0xf790) BEFORE the item sprites) so the menu-item bars behind the dialog are
erased.  0f1a (save-buffer RESERVE) calls the device-alloc vector [DGROUP:0xcc], UNINSTALLED in our port
(== 0, same gap class as patch 049's palette alloc / 134's 0xe4) -> no buffer, flag sign-bit never set ->
0f3a save-blit / 0fe4 restore-blit no-op -> item bars persisted.  0f1a reconstructed (asm 0xf1a): compute
the save size, resolve FUN_1000_182a directly to reserve the buffer into the save descriptor (writes
{seg,0xa0}); REUSE an already-reserved buffer so the per-frame menu save doesn't leak (the raw 182a
frees+reallocs via the 184b bit7 free-path, an unimplemented MEMMGR follow-on here).

List-box NAME text rendered as blocks: thunk_FUN_1000_5531 (the DGROUP-string glyph loop b631 uses)
dropped the AL char arg to the per-glyph blitter [0x684] -> every glyph a stale block.  Thread al (same
as the working 5591, patch 115).

Selection HIGHLIGHT (red bar on the selected row) missing: MGAVIDEO 0x10d1 (the masked highlight fill
that c60e dispatches) was unreconstructed ("Subroutine does not return", 1091/patch-060 class).
Reconstructed (asm 0x10d1..0x1113): masked fill = write AL except where pixel==AH (preserve).  b5a4's
call threaded to pass the full colour word ax=0x000e (AL=0xe red fill, AH=0 transparent key) so the black
glyph pixels survive the highlight.

Result: SELECT PLAYER AE = 0/64000 vs ref/selplayer_native320.png on native AND wasm, native<->wasm
0-diff, deterministic (normal + pattern-init).  No engine re_out/*.c change (fist.c pristine); patches
only fist.c + fist_mga.c via the build.  The 4 prior verify flows unchanged.

